{"id": "L10", "command": "submit", "inputs": {"recommendation": {"decision": "keep", "challenger": null, "diagnosis": "The champion's slight degradation over the development window comes mainly from the early-April shock in BR and MX; error has since returned to normal levels and current volatility is unremarkable. IN error rose relative to its unusually calm prior period, and the model carries a persistent tendency to forecast too high in BR and MX.", "evidence": [{"claim": "The champion's error over the last 26 weeks was 56.39 bps vs 55.34 bps before (+1.9%), with the last 4 weeks at 47.15 bps.", "ledger_ids": ["L02"]}, {"claim": "The champion's monthly error peaked at 89.27 bps in 2025-04 and was 47.15 bps in 2025-08; its bias was -11.84 bps in BR and -10.59 bps in MX.", "ledger_ids": ["L03"]}, {"claim": "Faster adaptation did not help: weekly refit scored 56.34 bps (-0.09%), and a 2y window with halflife 5 scored 58.78 bps (+4.24%).", "ledger_ids": ["L04", "L05"]}, {"claim": "Switching family gave no gain: LightGBM with the same features scored 56.59 bps (+0.35%) and the EWMA baseline 61.41 bps (+8.9%).", "ledger_ids": ["L06", "L07"]}, {"claim": "The best candidate, dropping FX-return and dollar-index features, scored 55.67 bps vs 56.39 bps (-1.28%), lower in every corridor but within normal development noise, and its BR bias stayed at -11.81 bps.", "ledger_ids": ["L08", "L09"]}], "risks": "The leaner feature set may hold a small real edge that we are leaving on the table, and the champion's monthly refit could lag if another sharp shock like April hits. The over-forecasting bias in BR and MX persists and is not fixed by any configuration tried.", "watch_next_week": "Re-check whether the leaner candidate's edge holds and stays consistent across corridors as the window rolls forward; watch IN error and the BR and MX bias, and revisit faster refit if volatility percentiles jump."}}, "result": {"accepted": true, "errors": [], "attempt": 1}, "time": "2026-11-15T11:4